Well, not as clear as it could be.

We've rolled a group of OpenVMS nodes forward to y2k for testing purposes.
Certainly any batch jobs scheduled to run sometime in 1999 would start
executing as soon as you changed the system date into 2000.  Stop the queues
($ STOP/QUEUE q_name) if this is a problem, put them on hold, or modify them
to a new start time.

The only repercussions we saw were:

    1) Jobs that archive/delete old data did so - based on the system's y2k
date - so we purged a lot of data all at once
    2)  When we reset the date to 1999, we had a bunch of files with 2000
dates on them - which cause the occassional hiccup in some DCL that
manages/purges flat files.

Other than that - pretty darn smooth.

ws



